@robertkirkman That requirement creates an unexpected deadlock due to how users interact on GitHub. 

When users search for a package and find an active, open PR like this one, they almost never comment "I need this"—they simply assume it's already being handled by the maintainers and wait for it to land. A real example of this is PR #29412 (OBS Studio), which has been open for months; despite user interest, no one leaves "I need this" comments on active PRs as standard practice is to avoid spamming pull requests.

Since the packages are fully built, passing CI, and follow standard Arch/Repology naming, I'll keep this PR open for now to see if anyone drops a comment or if you're open to merging a subset (like the 5-6 most popular ones). If it remains blocked, I can eventually move these to TUR for community access.

